@title Observability Stack for 2027
@subtitle Copperleaf Insurance SRE comparison for the budget meeting

# Context

We run 340 hosts, ingest about 2.1 TB of logs per month, and have 14 engineers on call. We are choosing between Datadog, Grafana Cloud, and a self-hosted stack of Prometheus, Loki and Grafana on our own Kubernetes.

# Comparison table

table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,low,excellent,excellent,high,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,low,good,good,medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,high,good,fair,low,"$148,000 plus 1.5 engineers"

# Three-year cost

data cum = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004

chart line cum x=year y=Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted unit=k title="Cumulative cost in thousands of dollars, including staff time for self-hosted"

# Pros and cons

### Datadog

- Pros: excellent alerting and log search, low setup effort
- Cons: highest annual cost, high lock-in

### Grafana Cloud

- Pros: low setup effort, dashboards stay portable, cheapest once staff time is counted
- Cons: log search is only good, not excellent

### Self-hosted

- Pros: lowest lock-in, lowest license cost
- Cons: high setup effort, log search is fair, needs 1.5 engineers we have not hired

# Recommendation

Grafana Cloud. It is the cheapest option once staff time is counted, and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30.

! Self-hosted assumes we can hire the 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
